---
const faqs = [
	{
		question:
			'If my device is not listed under "Works with Home Assistant" does this mean it\'s not supported?',
		answer:
			"No! It just means it hasn't gone through a testing schedule with our team, or doesn't fit the program requirements. It might function well, but be added to the testing schedule later down the road, it could be missing a function or firmware, or it might work under a different connectivity type that we don't currently test under the program.",
	},
	{
		question: "OK, so what's the point of the Works with program?",
		answer:
			"It highlights the devices we know work well with Home Assistant and the brands that make a long-term commitment to supporting these devices. The certification agreement specifies the devices must have key functionality within Home Assistant and operate locally without the need for cloud – both now and in the future.",
	},
	{
		question: "What about this missing product?",
		answer:
			"Some partners are missing as they expand their product lines and testing takes place. We will be consistently working to keep this up-to-date.",
	},
	{
		question: "How is this work funded?",
		answer:
			"This program is non-commercial and made possible thanks to the generous support of our Home Assistant Cloud subscribers.",
	},
	{
		question: "Are these affiliate links?",
		answer:
			"No, to respect the privacy of our users, this list does not use affiliate links.",
	},
];
---

<div class="faq-section">
	<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

	<div class="faq-accordion">
		{
			faqs.map((faq) => (
				<details class="faq-item">
					<summary class="faq-question">
						<span>{faq.question}</span>
						<span class="faq-icon">
							<svg
								viewBox="0 0 24 24"
								fill="none"
								stroke="currentColor"
								stroke-width="2"
								stroke-linecap="round"
								stroke-linejoin="round"
							>
								<polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9" />
							</svg>
						</span>
					</summary>
					<div class="faq-answer">
						<p>{faq.answer}</p>
					</div>
				</details>
			))
		}
	</div>
</div>
